<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Indonesia coal terminal work faces 4-month delay.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Indonesia coal terminal work faces 4-month delay.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Damage caused by a storm will delay completion of a coal loading terminal in Pulau Laut, Indonesia by up to four months until September 1997, the consulting engineers to the project, Washington H. Soul Pattinson &amp; Co Ltd said on Monday</p>
<p>On Dec 11, a barge broke loose from its mooring in high seas, and caused extensive damage to the piles in the inshore export wharf of the terminal.</p>
<p>It will take six weeks to deliver replacement piles to the site and as much as a further 10 weeks to re-drive the piles, the firm said.  </p>
<p>It estimated the cost of the damage at between US$2</p>
<p>million and $3 million.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
